diff --git a/specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md b/specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..619b1a2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Shipped              |
+
+Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.
+
+## Validation at execute time
+
+- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16)).
+- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
+- When `input` supplies a property whose value is not in the declared `enum` list, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` rejecting the value without invoking the executor ([validated by: rejects input with enum validation failure](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L233)).
+- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults ([validated by: passes valid input through to executor unchanged including extra properties](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L9)).
+- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake ([validated by: throws Unknown tool for unregistered tools](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L4)).
+
+## Schema compilation and caching
+
+- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: compiles a static tool schema once across ten execute calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L42)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules ([validated by: validates function-valued schema against the current definition, not a stale cached schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L67)).
+
+## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery
+
+- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).
+
+## Registry helper methods
+
+- `ToolRegistry.get(name)` returns the registered tool's definition and executor wrapper when the tool has been registered, and `undefined` when it has not ([validated by: returns registered tool with definition and executor for get](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L103) and [validated by: returns undefined for get on unregistered tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L130)).
+- `ToolRegistry.has(name)` returns `true` for a registered tool and `false` for an unregistered tool ([validated by: has returns true for registered tools and false for unregistered](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L136)).
+- `ToolRegistry.getDefinitions()` returns an array of all registered tool definitions in the order they were registered ([validated by: getDefinitions returns all registered tool definitions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L156)).
+- `ToolRegistry.getPromptInstructions()` returns only the prompt instructions from tools that have declared `promptInstructions`, formatted as `tool_name: instruction_text` ([validated by: getPromptInstructions returns instructions for tools with promptInstructions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L185)).
+- `ToolRegistry.getExamplePrompts()` returns a flattened array of all example prompts from all registered tools, preserving order ([validated by: getExamplePrompts returns flattened example prompts from tools](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L209)).
